This directory (src-tauri/src/echo_cancel/) is an independent Rust
implementation whose *architecture* -- a delay estimator, a partitioned
frequency-domain adaptive filter, echo-path/ERLE tracking, a residual
echo estimator, a suppression gain with a comfort floor, and a
double-talk-aware adaptation controller -- is modeled on the publicly
documented design of WebRTC's AEC3 (modules/audio_processing/aec3 in
the WebRTC source tree, https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src, also
mirrored on GitHub). No AEC3 source code was copied; this is not a
line-by-line port. The above notice is included, and this file kept
alongside the code it describes, purely as attribution for that
architectural debt, in the spirit of the BSD-3-Clause terms under
which AEC3 itself is published. See docs/transcription.md for what is
simplified relative to full AEC3 (e.g. a single linear filter stage
rather than AEC3's separate refined/coarse filters, and a coarse
energy-ratio double-talk detector rather than a coherence-based one).
